cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  LitUbik: an open-source, AI-assisted workbench covering the full
  systematic-review lifecycle, from registered protocol to PRISMA 2020
message: If you use LitUbik in a review, please cite it.
type: software
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
repository-code: https://github.com/abequet/litubik_public
abstract: >-
  LitUbik is a self-hosted web application covering the complete
  systematic-review lifecycle: import of a pre-registered protocol,
  construction and multi-database translation of search equations, automated
  database searching, fuzzy deduplication, blinded multi-reviewer screening of
  titles/abstracts and full texts, full-text retrieval, citation snowballing,
  quality appraisal (JBI, MMAT), data extraction, and a live PRISMA 2020 flow
  diagram.
  Optional large-language-model assistance is available at every stage, always
  subject to human validation and recorded with full provenance.
keywords:
  - systematic literature review
  - PRISMA 2020
  - evidence synthesis
  - research methodology
  - large language models
  - reproducibility
authors:
  - family-names: Béquet
    given-names: Adolphe J.
    affiliation: Université Gustave Eiffel
  - family-names: Laurent
    given-names: Sébastien
    affiliation: Independent web developer
